<title>USA: Costa Rica free of exotic Newcastle disease--USDA.</title>
<headline>Costa Rica free of exotic Newcastle disease--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Wednesday it had declared Costa Rica free of exotic Newcastle disease, a contagious and fatal viral disease that affects birds.</p>
<p>No case of the disease has been confirmed in Costa Rica in the past five years.</p>
<p>The declaration would allow poultry and poultry products to be shipped from Costa Rica to the United States under certain conditions, USDA said.</p>
<p>The declation was to become effective June 6.</p>
